{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c56f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d595-9c87-7b41-8174-a6b1261d78d7"},"sequence":274,"recorded_at":1780531400000543,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d596-6cce-7f40-90cd-18f663bc823b"},"task_id":"01a0d596-6cce-7f40-90cd-18f663bc823b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d596-6cce-7f40-90cd-18f663bc823b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"W=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree\\npython3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('$W/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json'))\\nprint('acceptance_cases:', len(d['acceptance_cases']))\\nprint('ownership rows:', len(d['ownership']))\\nprint('unowned:', d.get('unowned_sections'))\\nfor o in d['ownership']:\\n    s=str(o)\\n    if '13.14' in s or 'fidelity' in s.lower() or 'clone' in s.lower():\\n        print(json.dumps(o)[:800]); print('---')\\n\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 80\",\n  \"description\": \"Find clone rows in registry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"acceptance_cases: 163\\nownership rows: 77\\nunowned: [{'key': 'section:18.4', 'gap': 'Section 18.4 requires audit retention - the exact Section 5.2 event types for lease change, force confirmation, managed replacement, task-board launch and adoption and tombstone issuance and resolution, and retention of the event and every referenced immutable object for as long as the Session Record. No retention, expiry or garbage-collection rule is implemented.', 'evidence': 'internal/localstore/projection.go opens, rebuilds and recovers the SQLite projection and installs immutable blobs; it declares no retention, expiry or garbage-collection behaviour, and the binding this entry replaces named OpenProjection with the same two storage acceptance cases already used by the Section 3.3 binding.'}, {'key': 'section:11.10.5', 'gap': 'Section 11.10.5 defines the upstream public synthetic admission validator, not a runtime requirement to parse SPEC.md during AX host admission. TASK-260830-2x16gz consumes its vectors as source evidence only and implements no policy reader; synthetic passes never establish executed product support. Disclosure owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.', 'evidence': 'The pinned section explicitly calls the predicates synthetic execution context and separates detailed DER, custody and runtime boundaries from policy witnesses. No policy-reader declaration exists in the tree; production host-channel admission is proven by the AC-HOST-001 suite over the real Dial/Serve/Call entries instead.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.1', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.1 requires literal first-at source-qualified selector grammar with configured source-index resolution; no selector parser or source index exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-21gygk.', 'evidence': 'No CLI session commands exist at all: the tree builds no ax binary, sessadapter SourceSelector validates directory-protocol members rather than CLI selectors, and Section 2.3 name precedence is shape validation only.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.2', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.2 requires resolve-once fact binding with revalidation before execution; no selection planner or bound-fact store exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-21gygk.', 'evidence': 'Nothing binds selection facts to execution: there is no selector resolver whose output could go stale, and no plan revalidation reads a source index.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.3', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.3 binds the five Structured Error 1.4.0 codes to exits exclusively inside CLI Result 5; no Go mapping carries those codes. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1i7bqr.', 'evidence': 'The axerror registry is closed over Structured Error 1.0.0 through 1.3.0 with 109 codes; the 1.4.0 code-to-exit mapping has no implementation and no emitter.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.4', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.4 requires interrupted record-only creation with authoritative bootstrap recovery; no chooser, bootstrap creation or recovery flow exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1wb06o.', 'evidence': 'No session creation path exists in the tree: there is no CLI create command, no chooser, and no bootstrap lease issuance that an interruption could leave record-only.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.5', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.5 defines the upstream selector publication evaluator and its source-only case inventory. Source publication does not attest runtime provenance, temporal boundaries or running AX implementation; product selector conformance remains pending. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1i7bqr.', 'evidence': 'The pinned section explicitly distinguishes the publication evaluator from runtime authority/durability obligations. Upstream source publication ownership remains agent-session-manager-spec; TASK-260830-1i7bqr owns product-level composed conformance using the shared resolver and lifecycle APIs.'}]\\n{\\\"kind\\\": \\\"contract\\\", \\\"keys\\\": [\\\"Configuration [urn:ax:schema:config]\\\", \\\"Provider protocol [urn:ax:protocol:provider]\\\", \\\"Provider manifest [urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest]\\\", \\\"Provider probe [urn:ax:schema:provider-probe]\\\", \\\"Terminal Backend protocol [urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend]\\\", \\\"Terminal Backend manifest [urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest]\\\", \\\"Terminal Backend probe [urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe]\\\", \\\"Terminal Instance binding [urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding]\\\", \\\"Terminal capability evidence [urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence]\\\", \\\"Session Adapter protocol [urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter]\\\", \\\"Sessio