{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c65b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d595-9c87-7b41-8174-a6b1261d78d7"},"sequence":392,"recorded_at":1780531400000779,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d596-c204-7e62-8994-d6f3b8b76b2d"},"task_id":"01a0d596-c204-7e62-8994-d6f3b8b76b2d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d596-c204-7e62-8994-d6f3b8b76b2d","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree/internal/clonereadback/sealed.go`.\n1|package clonereadback\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file seals validated read-back manifests (SPEC v0.7.0\n8|// Section 13.14.2 lines 10753-10763: the validation report\n9|// aggregates TWO DISTINCT validated staged and live read-back\n10|// manifests). A report entry cannot vouch for a sibling from a\n11|// caller-minted struct that merely repeats an ID and a mode\n12|// label: every other field could be zero without any validated\n13|// read-back bytes behind it. Parse, don't validate: the report\n14|// entries accept ONLY ValidatedReadBack, a value the read-back\n15|// validator mints and no outside caller can forge — its fields\n16|// are unexported, the only constructors are the two read-back\n17|// entries, and the zero value is refused at both report entries.\n18|// The sealed value carries the validated manifest (with the\n19|// omit-self digest set and the ReadAuthority-derived mode) behind\n20|// read-only accessors; the accessors return scalars and a struct\n21|// copy, never a new seal.\n22|\n23|// ValidatedReadBack is one sealed read-back manifest: proof that\n24|// the read passed the read-back validator. The zero value seals\n25|// nothing and every report entry refuses it.\n26|type ValidatedReadBack struct {\n27|\tread   ReadBackManifest\n28|\tsealed bool\n29|}\n30|\n31|// sealReadBack mints one sealed read from a validated manifest.\n32|// Only the read-back entries call it, after every gate passes.\n33|func sealReadBack(read ReadBackManifest) ValidatedReadBack {\n34|\treturn ValidatedReadBack{read: read, sealed: true}\n35|}\n36|\n37|// Manifest returns the validated manifest behind the seal: a\n38|// struct copy for field reads. The copy cannot mint a seal —\n39|// only the read-back entries seal — so handing it out changes no\n40|// gate.\n41|func (v ValidatedReadBack) Manifest() ReadBackManifest {\n42|\treturn v.read\n43|}\n44|\n45|// ManifestID returns the sealed omit-self digest.\n46|func (v ValidatedReadBack) ManifestID() scalar.Digest {\n47|\treturn v.read.ManifestID\n48|}\n49|\n50|// Mode returns the sealed ReadAuthority-derived mode.\n51|func (v ValidatedReadBack) Mode() string {\n52|\treturn v.read.Mode\n53|}","final_result":true}}}
