{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e72f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d595-9c87-7b41-8174-a6b1261d78d7"},"sequence":4594,"recorded_at":1780531400009183,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f52b624-2d68-419d-80a5-f0df2f588e41"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d5be-6186-7012-af82-6843ddc3968f"},"task_id":"01a0d5be-6186-7012-af82-6843ddc3968f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d5be-6186-7012-af82-6843ddc3968f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-111-1\",\n  \"command\": \"W=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree\\nhead -n 40 \\\"$W/LOGBOOK.md\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Read LOGBOOK head format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-24\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2h5uv9 rev5 — always-on common-ID position product\\n\\n- The configured generated sync test now runs its N≤3 bounded shard without a selector. A separate always-on 432-case production `DurableIndex.SyncFrom` product places a same-identity/different-bytes conflict at each of three sorted common-ID positions, crossed with all six arrival permutations, duplicate on/off, both skews, rounds 1–3, and two peer-only lease identities. It asserts literal `integrity_failure`, quarantine bytes, peer immutability, and conflict on retry.\\n- Added AST skip census (zero unallowlisted skips), ordinary and token-preserving planted-skip refusals, and repository-root `.pyc`/`__pycache__` hygiene plus planted-artifact refusal. Removed the task-owned scratch Python cache; the focused selected tests and determinism run are green.\\n- The four review narrowings—first namespace, first ID, last ID, even IDs only—are killed alone by `TestDurableSyncConflictAuditsEveryCommonIDPositionWithPeerOnlyRecord`; each rework plant was run in a targeted invocation and in the 86-row shipped harness. The token-preserving skip plant is killed by `TestSkipCensusRejectsAnUnjustifiedPlantedSkip`. The applied neutral comment control survives. Harness results: 85 kills, one control survivor, zero invalid rows.\\n- Registry decode confirms all three Story acceptance cases occur in their declared clause bindings and names `SyncFrom` production ownership; digest re-derives to `2302a10a0174ada997614ea7d6112add30e9b2328f6b25ea796ea175f48568cd`. Tracecheck is green; README pin passes and the wrong-figure plant fails. Scoped diagnostics refuse at §5.3 (7/8), §10.7 (1/18), and §11.4 (6/7), as expected for the stated task boundary.\\n- Exact `go list -test -json` comparison: fork base `0ca3e4c` to candidate is 44→46 package paths, 1,468→1,592 references, and 317→350 internal references; tracked target importer union is 25→27 with no removed target edges. New target callers are `merkleinventory` for canonicaljson/rpcwire and test-only `tmuxserver` for provhost. Base importer execution is reused from its immutable green evidence; all 27 candidate importers are in the exact candidate suite.\\n- Focused package gate, final `-count=3` determinism gate, exact full configured suite (46/46 packages), Windows vet, gofmt, build, tracecheck, scratch-index diff check, and `task-board.config.json` byte comparison all have green evidence after the repository-root bytecode hygiene change. The final full suite and determinism process exited 0; raw output is attached and read back.\\n- Measured task acceptance ratio remains 1 of 2 criteria fully driven by named tests; the no-public-capability clause is a stated scope bound because this internal library adds no public advertisement entry point. The producer brief has no formal surface table; `coverage-map.md` records this as a brief gap. Candidate remains uncommitted at the Story checkpoint; current origin main is still `6d3bff9`.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2h5uv9 rev4 — partial-overlap conflict crossed with generated sync product\\n\\n- Rework adds generated same-ID/different-bytes cases beside peer-only identities across reorder, duplicate, gap-fill, both clock skews, partial peer, and rounds 1–3. The review reproduction is named in `TestDurableSyncConflictWithPartialOverlapPeer`; an AST check guards unconditional common-ID audit. Product audit: 38,000 valid + 37,765 conflict cases; N1–N5 full, N6 34 samples. All successful selector ranges are attached; two wide N6 selectors timed out and were rerun successfully in smaller non-overlapping selectors.\\n- Validation on this candidate: full `go test ./... -count=1`, Windows vet, build, diff check, tracecheck, determinism `-count=3`, and README coverage pin all exit 0. Wrong README figure plant exits 1 as expected. Mutation harness: 83 rows, 81 narrowing kills, one token-preserving behavior kill, one applied neutral control survivor; no NOT_APPLIED rows. Registry digest `cf559de0d70bf68546b12169ff30549022d106939d9dab71ac691fa260b34c80`.\\n- Rework evidence gap: this run did not rerun the fork-base importer outcome grid, section-scoped tracecheck diagnostics, standalone digest plant, or lint. Candidate importer consumers were exercised in the full suite. The brief has no formal surface table; N=6 permutations are sampled. See attached results for bounds and exit codes.\\n\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2h5uv9 — story-final handoff evidence refreshed\\n\\n- CHANGE REQUEST: Earlier revision 1/2 command 4/30 evidence was truncated at 65,536 bytes and reports `failure_class=unknown`; no failure cause is inferred. The exact-tree bounded configured suite now exits 0 across 46/46 packages, with the generated property separately completed in 47 exact selectors.\\n- PROPERTY: `TestDurableSyncGeneratedPerturbationProduct` drives production `DurableIndex.SyncFrom` over 38,000 cases. N=1..5 arrival permutations are exhaustive; N=6 samples 34 unique orders. Every case crosses duplicate on/off, both opposing timestamp assignments, no-gap/delayed fill, compatible partial-peer subsets, and one-to-three sync passes. Independent root/projection oracles require convergence or literal typed `integrity_failure`; all 47 accepted processes exit 0. Whole-store bytes are identical after repeat sync.\\n- MUTANTS: The 77-row current harness has 75 ordinary narrowing kills, one token-preserving behavioral narrowing killed by `TestClassifyRefusesIdentityDigestMismatch`, and one applied neutral comment control survivor. No gate mutant is arm-delete. Per-plant logs/table are in the task evidence archive.\\n- REGISTRY: Decoded all three Story leaves' clause edges; `10.7#13` now includes `story-260830-2h5uv9-order-duplicate-gap-convergence` in both the section binding and clause acceptance list. Registry regression checks defined cases against decoded clause lists. The expected-red digest probe exited 1 while surfacing `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256=22bc6b0037c011385fee7d92ebe268bb36a1413341a4d0a5e4b60490d16fd2e0`; after repinning, exact tracecheck exited 0. It reports 64 contracts, 36 normative sections, 163 acceptance cases, 33 fixtures, 55 compatibility contracts; `bindings=72 full=4 partial=11 sliver=12 unevidenced=41 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=88/610`. The README coverage pin is green. Scoped diagnostics are expected-red: §10.7 1/18, §11.4 6/7, §5.3 7/8.\\n- IMPORTERS: Compared exact fork base `0ca3e4c26e2b275212796657f785b9b450f6174e` with candidate: 44→46 package paths, 1,468→1,591 direct refs, 317→350 internal refs; +123/+33 and no removals. Added paths are `merkleinventory` and `tmuxserver`. The exact 25-package fork-base importer set passed (8,967 test events); candidate target importers are among 46/46 green configured packages. Exact input grid and moved classes are bundled.\\n- VALIDATION: Candidate `go test ./... -count=1 -v`, `go test ./internal/merkleinventory -count=1 -v`, traceability and tracecheck package tests, `go build ./...`, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, `golangci-lint run --new ./...`, exact tracecheck, and final diff/gofmt checks have real exit 0. Section-scoped tracecheck commands exit 1 as expected and are retained as diagnostics, not green gates. No previously committed task-scope test was removed or renamed; task-package reviewer tests are green in the configured suite/property shards.\\n- BASE / BOUNDS: Current origin main was observed at `6d3bff999f75ed8585a7ef32074ab108f364ec51`; it remains an ancestor and no candidate refresh was needed. N=6 order coverage is sampled, the largest measured set is N=6, and repeated sync is measured through three rounds plus a post-convergence no-op. The brief has no formal surface table; the coverage map reports this gap. Raw-blob transfer, lifecycle effects, lease issuance/takeover, retention, and physical power loss remain unclaimed. Candidate changes remain uncommitted at the Story checkpoint.\\n- HANDOFF ARTIFACTS: Attached and read back `_results.md`, `_conformance-matrix.md`, and `_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (412,702 bytes, 311 entries); all byte hashes match their worktree sources. The archive includes all 47 property logs and all mutation overlays/raw logs. The full configured-suite log (396,512-byte gzip) and exact fork-base importer event log (616,812-byte gzip) are separate task-scoped outcome resources and also read back byte-identically.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-g0pcnt rev6 revalidation — path-derived length forms\\n\\n- TRANSITIVE GUARD: Extended the test-only AST taint analysis to keep path provenance through `strings.Split`, range indices over path components, numeric length/count expressions, and `[]byte(path)` conversions. The generator still sweeps the physical Darwin limit; the extra guard now rejects structural caps expressed as split-component count, range index, or byte length as well as direct separator/depth comparisons.\\n- MUTANTS: Added `N-ancestor-walk-split-component-count-cap`, `N-ancestor-walk-range-index-cap`, and `N-ancestor-walk-byte-length-cap`; each was run alone twice and each produced a raw Go test exit 1 with its named ancestor-walk test failing. `callee24` and `isFilesystemRoot` cap mutants were also rerun alone twice after the final guard edit and killed. An applied line-count-preserving `C-control` survived. The first range-index plant attempt failed to link with `no space left on device`; it was excluded, then two isolated retries killed it.\\n- VALIDATION: All 45 packages passed the configured verbose test gate in ten current bounded groups, all 45 passed coverage in ten current groups, and all 17 configured fuzz runs passed. Race groups passed for all packages except `sessquery`, whose current ten-minute-bounded attempt was interrupted at 9:48 (real exit 1, no test failure output); the prior rev6 `sessquery` race result (409.416s, exit 0) is reused because this revalidation changed only tmuxserver tests and the Python mutant harness, not that package or its production dependencies. The current tmuxserver race and coverage groups both exited 0. Determinism rerun of custody tests at `-count=3`, build, native vet, Windows vet/build, tracecheck, catalog check, JSON parse, task-board validate, and diff check exited 0. A monolithic `go test ./... -count=1 -v` attempt was interrupted (real exit 1); the complete package set passed in the bounded groups instead.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10495,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2624,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
